  "description": "Whenever he steps foot outside, Do-Jun is faced with an unexpected challenge – the seemingly never-ending public displays of affection from his next-door neighbors! But the fact that they’re both men means that Do-Jun’s discomfort quickly earns him the label of homophobe. Determined to break free from stereotypes, Do-Jun attempts to bridge the gap by reaching out to his neighbor, only to find himself entangled in far more than neighborly relations.\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)\n\n*Note: Includes five side story chapters.*",
